{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Cut CI tickets-store transfer cost across both checkout mechanisms. Measured evidence in session_log 1cb6-d553-6565-49b4 and epic comments: recurring actions/checkout full checkout 1.04 GiB / 59 s versus blob:none 68.7 MiB / 14.3 s; Gerrit verify-identity full tickets fetch 6.73 minutes, with local full 1.4 GB / 66.2 s versus blob:none 22 MB / 3.6 s and 83 MB / 8.6 s after worktree materialization. These are recorded baselines, not substitutes for the runtime guards below.\n\n## Scope and mechanisms\nAdd the documented actions/checkout v7 filter input (confirmed in the published actions/checkout action.yml; input name filter, available since v4.1.0) while retaining fetch-depth: 0 and existing credentials/ref settings in .github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml, .github/workflows/verify-identity.yml, and .github/workflows/reconcile-bridge-canary.yml. These all-history checkouts currently fetch the tickets branch before the later mount step.\n\nA subsequent plain git fetch origin +tickets must inherit the named remote filter. Config presence is insufficient because Git records partialclonefilter even when a server ignores it. Prove the actual protocol and missing-object behavior with a real server.\n\nIn .github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml, named-remote inheritance does not apply because both tickets fetches use a direct URL. Add --filter=blob:none explicitly to the depth-1 require-ticket fetch and to the full-history verify-identity fetch, preserving their different depth semantics. blob:none retains the complete commit graph needed by merge-base and era scoping; depth remains forbidden only on the identity fetch.\n\n## Real-Git fixture and safety\nIntegration tests start git daemon as a localhost subprocess with --export-all and --enable=upload-pack, serve a bare repo configured uploadpack.allowFilter=true, reserve a loopback port, and poll the socket with a bounded deadline before use. Do not use a file URL, whose filter behavior varies by Git version.\n\nThe fixture commits an incompressible historical blob larger than 140 MiB, then removes it and leaves a small tickets tip. After server-side gc, a full all-history fetch must exceed 131072 KiB while blob:none must remain below 102400 KiB before worktree materialization and below 131072 KiB after materializing only the small tip. This exact-threshold contrast makes the production guard logic executable rather than a YAML-presence assertion. Execute the actual named workflow run blocks against these repositories so a broken numeric comparison or KiB parse fails the integration test.\n\nCapture GIT_TRACE_PACKET for three fetch modes: plain named-origin inheritance, direct URL with --depth=1 --filter=blob:none, and direct URL full-history with --filter=blob:none. Each trace must contain fetch> filter blob:none, and a known tickets blob must be absent before worktree materialization.\n\nNever use filter: tree:0: measured 3.57 GiB across 2,255 promisor packs. git worktree add uses unpack-trees -u/check_updates and batch-prefetches missing promisor blobs, unlike the read-tree plus checkout-index footgun documented in tests/unit/test_snapshot_blobless_747f.py. A real-Git E2E must materialize tickets, create independent local and remote changes, fetch/merge with the B3 ours driver, retain all expected events, and push successfully.\n\n## Production guardrails\n- Standalone verify-identity: immediately after actions/checkout parse size-pack from git count-objects -v and fail above 102400 KiB.\n- Gerrit verify-identity: after filtered tickets fetch and worktree materialization fail above 131072 KiB. This runs on the patchset and proves the GitHub server honored the direct filter.\n- In both verify-identity jobs, snapshot exact git count-objects -v after materialization, run rebar verify-identity, snapshot again, and fail if any line differs. Materialization may fetch tip blobs; identity scanning must add no objects or packs.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Each of the three target actions/checkout@v7 steps sets filter: blob:none and retains fetch-depth: 0 plus its pre-existing credential/ref inputs. Tier: parsed workflow contract. Proving command: pytest tests/unit/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone_workflows.py -k checkout_inputs -v.\n- [ ] The depth-1 Gerrit require-ticket fetch passes --filter=blob:none and still passes --depth=1; the Gerrit identity fetch passes --filter=blob:none and has no depth option. Tier: parsed workflow contract. Proving command: pytest tests/unit/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone_workflows.py -k direct_fetch_inputs -v.\n- [ ] The production size guards parse size-pack from git count-objects -v and enforce exactly 102400 KiB for standalone checkout and 131072 KiB for Gerrit materialized tickets. Tier: parsed executable workflow contract. Proving command: pytest tests/unit/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone_workflows.py -k size_pack -v.\n- [ ] Executing the actual workflow size-guard blocks against a real Git fixture rejects the unfiltered full-history repository above 131072 KiB and accepts the blobless repository below 102400 KiB before materialization. Tier: real-Git contrast integration. Proving command: pytest tests/integration/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone.py -k size_pack -v.\n- [ ] The same real-Git size-guard execution accepts the blobless materialized small tickets tip below 131072 KiB. Tier: real-Git boundary integration. Proving command: pytest tests/integration/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone.py -k materialized_size_pack -v.\n- [ ] Plain named-origin fetch inheritance emits fetch> filter blob:none and leaves a known tickets blob missing before materialization. Tier: real Git protocol. Proving command: pytest tests/integration/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone.py -k named_origin_filter -v.\n- [ ] Both direct-URL fetch modes emit fetch> filter blob:none and leave a known tickets blob missing before materialization. Tier: real Git protocol. Proving command: pytest tests/integration/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone.py -k direct_fetch_filter -v.\n- [ ] A blobless tickets worktree reconverges independent local and remote changes with the configured ours driver, retains every expected event, and pushes the merged result. Tier: real-Git end to end. Proving command: pytest tests/integration/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone.py -k reconverges -v.\n- [ ] In both production identity jobs exact git count-objects -v output is identical immediately before and after rebar verify-identity. Tier: executable workflow plus real-Git integration. Proving commands: pytest tests/unit/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone_workflows.py -k no_promisor -v and pytest tests/integration/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone.py -k verify_identity_no_promisor -v.\n\n## Files and rollback\nFiles: .github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml; .github/workflows/verify-identity.yml; .github/workflows/reconcile-bridge-canary.yml; .github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml; tests/unit/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone_workflows.py; tests/integration/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone.py.\n\nRollback is one Gerrit revert of this change, restoring the prior full-fetch behavior and removing the paired guards. Do not disable only a failing size guard: a threshold trip means the cost regression is real until the filter/server path is repaired or the whole optimization is reverted.\n\nScope: M. Depends on closed B3 040e-3f0c-ae86-4212 and closed B6 3036-cb14-86b5-44a3."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785611617961944001,"uuid":"0ff1feac-5a8e-4674-b8f5-b6240dd31ef2"}